<title>USA: Triton to explore offshore Equitorial Guinea.</title>
<headline>Triton to explore offshore Equitorial Guinea.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triton Energy Corp said Friday that it recently signed a production sharing agreement to explore acreage offshore Equitorial Guinea.</p>
<p>Dallas-based Triton said it has the right to explore for oil in two offshore blocks, G and F, located 250 kilometers southeast of the capital Malabo. The blocks cover approximately 1.3 million acres.</p>
<p>Triton is operator and holds a 100 percent interest in the exploration blocks.</p>
<p>The company plans shortly to reprocess some existing seismic data and to shoot new data, a company spokesperson said.</p>
<p>(New York Energy Desk, + 1 212 859 1623)</p>
